{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 0, "result": {"protocolVersion": "2025-06-18", "capabilities": {"tools": {"listChanged": false}, "resources": {}, "prompts": {}}, "serverInfo": {"name": "ucas", "title": "ucas, a computer algebra system for programmers", "version": "1"}, "instructions": "ucas analyses functions (exhaustively on machine types), does exact algebra and calculus, transforms, number theory and finite fields, and finds cheaper implementations, each answer checked or proved.  Expressions are ucas syntax strings; give parameters types (x: u8, x: f32, x: real) where it matters.  Definitions persist across calls.  An ambiguous input is an error listing its readings: retry with args.assume.KEY.  structuredContent holds the typed result, checks and proof."}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Z/4 + Z/6 = Z/2 + Z/12: isomorphic, both Z/2 + Z/12\n  phi: (1, 0) -> (1, 3), (0, 1) -> (1, 2)\n  psi = phi^-1: (1, 0) -> (2, 3), (0, 1) -> (1, 5)\n  check: phi and psi are well defined (relations go to relations), psi phi = 1 and phi psi = 1 on generators\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 1, "ok": true, "cmd": "abiso", "ucas": "abiso Z/4 + Z/6, Z/2 + Z/12", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "abiso", "isomorphic": true, "phi_matrix": "[[1, 1], [3, 2]]", "psi_matrix": "[[-2, 1], [3, -1]]", "phi": "(1, 0) -> (1, 3), (0, 1) -> (1, 2)", "psi": "phi^-1: (1, 0) -> (2, 3), (0, 1) -> (1, 5)", "lhs": "Z/4 + Z/6", "value": "Z/2 + Z/12: isomorphic, both Z/2 + Z/12", "headline": "Z/4 + Z/6 = Z/2 + Z/12: isomorphic, both Z/2 + Z/12"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "phi and psi are well defined (relations go to relations), psi phi = 1 and phi psi = 1 on generators"}], "files": [], "text": "Z/4 + Z/6 = Z/2 + Z/12: isomorphic, both Z/2 + Z/12\n  phi: (1, 0) -> (1, 3), (0, 1) -> (1, 2)\n  psi = phi^-1: (1, 0) -> (2, 3), (0, 1) -> (1, 5)\n  check: phi and psi are well defined (relations go to relations), psi phi = 1 and phi psi = 1 on generators\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 2, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Smith normal form of the 3x3 matrix: diag(2, 6, 12), rank 3\n  D: [[2, 0, 0], [0, 6, 0], [0, 0, 12]]\n  U: [[1, 0, 0], [-1, 3, 2], [3, -4, -3]]\n  V: [[1, -2, -2], [0, 1, 0], [0, 0, 1]]\n  U^-1: [[1, 0, 0], [-3, 3, 2], [5, -4, -3]]\n  V^-1: [[1, 2, 2], [0, 1, 0], [0, 0, 1]]\n  cokernel: Z^3 / (columns) = Z/2 + Z/6 + Z/12\n  check: U A V = D, U U^-1 = I and V V^-1 = I (unimodular), d_i | d_(i+1): verified\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 2, "ok": true, "cmd": "snf", "ucas": "snf [[2, 4, 4], [-6, 6, 12], [10, -4, -16]]", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "snf", "diagonal": ["2", "6", "12"], "d": "[[2, 0, 0], [0, 6, 0], [0, 0, 12]]", "u": "[[1, 0, 0], [-1, 3, 2], [3, -4, -3]]", "v": "[[1, -2, -2], [0, 1, 0], [0, 0, 1]]", "u_1": "[[1, 0, 0], [-3, 3, 2], [5, -4, -3]]", "v_1": "[[1, 2, 2], [0, 1, 0], [0, 0, 1]]", "cokernel": "Z^3 / (columns) = Z/2 + Z/6 + Z/12", "headline": "Smith normal form of the 3x3 matrix: diag(2, 6, 12), rank 3"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "U A V = D, U U^-1 = I and V V^-1 = I (unimodular), d_i | d_(i+1): verified"}], "files": [], "text": "Smith normal form of the 3x3 matrix: diag(2, 6, 12), rank 3\n  D: [[2, 0, 0], [0, 6, 0], [0, 0, 12]]\n  U: [[1, 0, 0], [-1, 3, 2], [3, -4, -3]]\n  V: [[1, -2, -2], [0, 1, 0], [0, 0, 1]]\n  U^-1: [[1, 0, 0], [-3, 3, 2], [5, -4, -3]]\n  V^-1: [[1, 2, 2], [0, 1, 0], [0, 0, 1]]\n  cokernel: Z^3 / (columns) = Z/2 + Z/6 + Z/12\n  check: U A V = D, U U^-1 = I and V V^-1 = I (unimodular), d_i | d_(i+1): verified\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 3, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "A5: a permutation group of degree 5, order 60\n  generators: (1 2 3), (1 2 4), (1 2 5)\n  base: 1, 2, 3; basic orbit lengths 5 4 3 (the order is their product); 6 strong generators\n  orbits: {1, 2, 3, 4, 5} (transitive)\n  abelian: no\n  derived series (orders): 60\n  solvable: no\n  lower central series (orders): 60\n  nilpotent: no\n  centre: order 1\n  how: Schreier-Sims (deterministic): every Schreier generator of every level sifts to the identity\n  check: every generator sifts through the stabilizer chain and its word rebuilds it: verified\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 3, "ok": true, "cmd": "permgroup", "ucas": "permgroup A5", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "permgroup", "order_value": "60", "solvable_value": false, "generators": "(1 2 3), (1 2 4), (1 2 5)", "base": "1, 2, 3; basic orbit lengths 5 4 3 (the order is their product); 6 strong generators", "orbits": "{1, 2, 3, 4, 5} (transitive)", "abelian": "no", "derived_series_orders": "60", "solvable": "no", "lower_central_series_orders": "60", "nilpotent": "no", "centre": "order 1", "method": "Schreier-Sims (deterministic): every Schreier generator of every level sifts to the identity", "headline": "A5: a permutation group of degree 5, order 60"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "every generator sifts through the stabilizer chain and its word rebuilds it: verified"}], "files": [], "text": "A5: a permutation group of degree 5, order 60\n  generators: (1 2 3), (1 2 4), (1 2 5)\n  base: 1, 2, 3; basic orbit lengths 5 4 3 (the order is their product); 6 strong generators\n  orbits: {1, 2, 3, 4, 5} (transitive)\n  abelian: no\n  derived series (orders): 60\n  solvable: no\n  lower central series (orders): 60\n  nilpotent: no\n  centre: order 1\n  how: Schreier-Sims (deterministic): every Schreier generator of every level sifts to the identity\n  check: every generator sifts through the stabilizer chain and its word rebuilds it: verified\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 4, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "x^3 - 1 is in the ideal (grevlex, x > y > z, over Q)\n  certificate: x^3 - 1 = (x^2)*(x + y + z) + (-x)*(x*y + x*z + y*z) + (1)*(x*y*z - 1)\n  check: the combination multiplied out equals the polynomial\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 4, "ok": true, "cmd": "idealmember", "ucas": "idealmember x^3 - 1 in x + y + z, x*y + y*z + z*x, x*y*z - 1", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "idealmember", "member": true, "cofactors": ["x^2", "-x", "1"], "certificate": "x^3 - 1 = (x^2)*(x + y + z) + (-x)*(x*y + x*z + y*z) + (1)*(x*y*z - 1)", "headline": "x^3 - 1 is in the ideal (grevlex, x > y > z, over Q)"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "the combination multiplied out equals the polynomial"}], "files": [], "text": "x^3 - 1 is in the ideal (grevlex, x > y > z, over Q)\n  certificate: x^3 - 1 = (x^2)*(x + y + z) + (-x)*(x*y + x*z + y*z) + (1)*(x*y*z - 1)\n  check: the combination multiplied out equals the polynomial\n"}, "isError": false}}
